{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md at exact b188c7f3d4509a6ff277498a22f947d627e3ac9a on request/jam-room-r6, under promise git:sha1…5219771 on request git:sha1…3969c35\n\nJam room, revision 6 at b188c7f3d4509a6ff277498a22f947d627e3ac9a on request/jam-room-r6, for request 9ce8533f (its condition 4). Subject: notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md. Design only; nothing was run and no audio was listened to by the author. It replaces the note's story with plan 021's: a person hums a tune of a few seconds and then mouths or taps a rhythm; an agent at a synth works out the tune and fixes key, tempo and bar grid; further agents take bass, drums and a lead in arrival order, and the band answers at about 120 beats a minute. It keeps the timing model and the split between what is recorded and what is live, restated in main's terms, and walks each kept statement against the new story in two tables (12 timing rows and 14 record rows, with what changes). It lists nine platform gaps with owners as findings, not as jam work: nothing is deployed; no repository can be founded whole on main; a grant cannot be limited to one instrument; a refused act writes nothing, so a recorded refusal does not exist; live delivery sends the head only; a watcher who is not a member has no read; no packages are published; a scope has an entry budget, so a session cannot run without end; and the rules cannot be changed by members yet. Spike J0's first half is brought in as dated evidence with its limits: a plain pitch tracker with no model found 8 notes in the hummed tune; the in-page model found the same pitches in fragments and was slower; onset detection found about four hits a second; nobody has judged recognizability, because the judge is a person listening; a hosted audio model was not run; five phrases by two people are owed. The recommendation is provisional. Eight places where plan 021 or the spike note conflicts with the kept design are listed for the planner, among them: the plan binds a pattern to a named bar where the kept rule derives the bar; the plan says a refusal is recorded; and the plan says the jam needs nothing new beyond the I3 scope. Dropped, with the earlier text left in revision 5: the sample library, the MIDI keyboard, typed signals, solo passing and the old spikes' items. Limits: the four adopted design notes were not read; their revisions are stated as the builder gave them (contract 19, authority 26, lane forms 15, recovery 9); the lanes reference, the protocol guide, plans 016 to 020 and the spike's source were not read.","body":{"commit":"b188c7f3d4509a6ff277498a22f947d627e3ac9a","path":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md"}}